title: Slack tools cannot inspect huddles or transcripts
updated_at: "2026-11-02T09:04:56Z"
---
The assistant has no available Slack tools to browse huddles or retrieve their transcripts. Users cannot ask it about huddle content unless they manually provide transcripts. Add appropriate Slack access/tooling for listing or finding huddles and retrieving transcripts, with suitable permission and privacy boundaries.

Decision (2026-11-02 batch): Slack lane serial B835 -> B832 -> B833 because Slack APIs, connector tests and registrations overlap. Verify official Slack huddle/transcript surfaces before implementation; expose only supported workspace/user-authorized content, actionable scope errors, and truthful limits where private transcript APIs do not exist.

\nRetest (2026-11-02): Current source/runtime still has no registered Slack-specific tools or API methods for searching huddles or reading their transcript files; capabilities reports 57 tools without Slack tools. Slack API official File object docs now document huddle_transcript_file_id and huddle_transcription metadata, but entitlement/scopes and supported retrieval methods need verification. This may be implementable via Slack file search/access if authorized; don't assume huddle transcripts are categorically unavailable. No actual Slack workspace/API access was exercised, so end-to-end availability remains unverified. Source: https://docs.slack.dev/reference/objects/file-object/

Decision (primary-source research 2026-11-02): Slack public conversation/file object docs now expose huddle_thread.room references and conditional files.info huddle_transcription/huddle_transcript_file_id. Implement authorized bounded channel discovery then file hydration; distinguish real transcript, notes, previews and unavailable content. No generic Calls API/private endpoints/Discovery fallback. Research receipt in Slack lane slack-api-research.md; actual workspace capability remains untested.

Independent API/content review of689283e6 found P2: Slack conversations.history is_limited=true is omitted and terminal pagination can imply an exhaustive negative search despite plan-hidden history. Accepted: preserve explicit history visibility limit, separate pagination exhaustion from requested-window coverage, test empty/matching terminal limited pages, and document that cursor pagination cannot restore hidden history. Security/runtime independent review still pending; fixes will be bundled after aggregation. All builds/tests remote x-p35 only.

Independent security/runtime review of689283e6 found three additional accepted defects: P1 mid-turn queued steering bypasses the explicit drain boundary and may retain another users frozen admin/membership authority; P1 per-user session key selects different egress scopes from the verified room snapshot; P2 clearing the live bot credential leaves old frozen token reads enabled. Fix together with is_limited content finding, add real mocked turn-loop injection/room-scope/parsed-empty-config regressions, then both independent scoped rereviews. Shared session hook changes are now safe to coordinate because B831 has merged; keep integrations out of core and fail closed for unknown injected callers. No merge or B833 until PASS.

Completed:689283e6 plusfa649f5a merged as5acc74e0 after independent API/content and security reviews, fixes, and both scoped PASS verdicts. Real Slack ingress/snapshot authority, actual steering invalidation, matching frozen room/profile egress, inactive live credential denial, origin/target membership/guest/private-room gates, bounded discovery/hydration and truthful conditional transcript/history coverage. Remote lane56focused/7828quick/minimal/optimized/fmt passed; exact combined master gate7887 tests in64.824s plus make fmt-check passed x-p35. Early fake-token auth.test fixture incident disclosed/corrected; no real credential, content read or write involved. Live workspace transcript availability remains conditional/unverified; source delivery and tests are complete.